---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { features } from '../data/site';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<BaseLayout title="Features" description="Explore Inventatory's stock, rack, import, project, history, and scanner workflows, with links to practical documentation.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-intro"><h1>What Inventatory does</h1><p class="lead">Manage the parts you own, know where they are, and compare them with what your next project needs.</p></header>
    <p class="notice">These guides describe the inspected application source. The available release is a prerelease; consult its release notes for version-specific changes.</p>
    <div class="features">{features.map(feature => <section class="feature-section"><div><h2>{feature.title}</h2><a href={url(feature.href)}>Read the guide →</a></div><div><p>{feature.text}</p><ul>{feature.details.map(detail => <li>{detail}</li>)}</ul></div></section>)}</div>
    <section class="section prose"><h2>Current boundaries</h2><p>Inventatory is a public beta for Windows and Ubuntu Linux x86-64. Stock and history are stored locally. DigiKey enrichment, release checks, and scanner communication need their respective network connections.</p><p>Scan R1’s desktop integration is implemented, but public hardware and firmware availability has not been verified. Multi-user workflows, MCP integration, and additional vendor and CAD integrations are listed as future work in the application repository.</p><a href={url('/docs/scanner/status/')}>Scanner availability and documentation status →</a></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .features { margin-top: var(--space-12); }
  .feature-section { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr; gap: var(--space-12); padding-block: var(--space-8); border-top: var(--border) solid var(--divider); }
  .feature-section h2 { font-size: var(--text-lead); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .feature-section ul { color: var(--secondary); margin-bottom: 0; }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 44rem) { .feature-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-6); } }
</style>
